        <h3>POSSESSION OF THE FLAT/PLOT:</h3>
        <p>7.1 Schedule for possession of the said [Flat]: The DEVELOPER agrees and understands that timely delivery of possession of the Schedule B property to the VENDEE/S and the common areas to the Association of VENDEE/S or competent authority, as the case may be, is the essence of the Agreement. The DEVELOPER assures to hand over possession of the Schedule B property of the project by June-2028&#8217; and with a grace period of 6 months unless there is a delay or failure due to war, flood, drought, fire, cyclone, earthquake, or any other calamity caused by nature or any Court stay or government order affecting the regular development of the real estate project (&#8220;Force Majeure&#8221;). If, however, the completion of the Project is delayed due to Force Majeure conditions then the VENDEE/S agree that the DEVELOPER shall be entitled to the extension of time and delivery of possession of the Schedule B property, provided that such Force Majeure conditions are not of nature which make it impossible for the contract to be implemented. The VENDEE/S agree and confirm that, in the event it becomes impossible for the DEVELOPER to implement the project due to Force Majeure conditions, then this agreement shall stand terminated and the DEVELOPER shall refund to the VENDEE, the entire amount received by the DEVELOPER from this agreement within 90 days from that date. The DEVELOPER shall intimate the VENDEE/S about such termination at least thirty days prior to such termination. After refund of the money paid to the VENDEE/S, the VENDEE/S agree that he/she shall not have any rights, claims, etc. against the DEVELOPER and that the DEVELOPER shall be released and discharged from all its obligations and liabilities under this Agreement.</p>
        <p>7.2 Procedure for taking possession &#8211; The Developers/Promoters (i) upon applying for and upon the completion of the period prescribed for issuing the Occupancy Certificate under applicable building laws; or (ii) after obtaining the Occupancy Certificate from the competent authority, shall offer in writing the possession of the Apartment, to the Vendee, who has paid all the amounts in terms of this Agreement. The Vendee shall take possession within two months from the date of the said notice. The Vendee shall be liable to pay property tax from the date of the Registration of the Sale Deed in favour of the Vendee or Occupancy Certificate whichever is earlier.</p>
        <p>If the Vendee fails to take delivery within the time specified in the notice referred to in Clause 7.2 above, he shall be liable for payment of all on goings including maintenance charges, water and electricity charges, Corpus Fund etc. from the date of notice. The Vendee, after taking possession or in accordance with Clause 7.2, agrees to pay the maintenance charges as determined by the Developers/Association of Vendees.</p>
        <p>7.3 Failure of VENDEE/S to take possession of Flat/Schedule B property &#8211; Upon receiving a written intimation from the DEVELOPER as per Para 7.2, the VENDEE/S shall take possession of the Flat from the documentation as prescribed in this Agreement, and the DEVELOPER shall give possession of the flat to the VENDEE/S. In case, the VENDEE/S fails to take possession within the time provided in para 7.2, such VENDEE/S shall continue to be liable to pay maintenance charges as specified in para 7.2.</p>
        <p>7.4 Possession by the VENDEE/S- After obtaining the occupancy certificate and handing over physical possession of the flat to the VENDEE/S, it shall be the responsibility of the DEVELOPER to hand over the necessary documents and plans, including common areas, to the Association of VENDEE/S or the competent authority, as the case may be, as per the local laws. [Provided that, in absence of any local law, the DEVELOPER shall handover the necessary documents and plans, including common areas, to the Association of VENDEE/S or the competent authority, as the case may be, within thirty days after obtaining the completion certificate]. Whereas it is made clear, that the VENDEE(S) / Purchaser shall be permitted for house-warming of his/her Flat subject to the payment/clearance of all the pending amounts due to the Developer and after obtaining No-Objection Certificate from Developer/Builder only.</p>
        <p>7.5 Cancellation by VENDEE/S &#8211; The Vendee shall have the right to cancel/withdraw his allotment in the Project only as provided in the Act.</p>
        <p>Provided that, where the Vendee proposes to cancel/withdraw from the Project without any fault of the Developer/AGPA holder, the Developer/AGPA holder herein is entitled to deduct an amount of 10% of Total Sale Consideration towards penal charges or compensation/ damages from the amount collected by Developers /Promoters.</p>
        <p>The balance amount of money paid by the Vendee shall be returned by the Developer/AGPA holder to the Vendee within three months of such cancellation or at the time that the Developer/AGPA holder are able to resell the said Apartment to another purchaser, whichever is later.</p>
        <p>7.6 Transfer rights by Vendee(s)/Purchaser(s):</p>
        <p>The Vendee(s)/Purchaser(s) is/are not allowed to sell / re-sell /transfer/ alienate his rights or assign or otherwise nominate a third party in any manner whatsoever till Two years from the date of Agreement of sale or the project is completed in full, whichever is later.</p>
        <p>The Vendee shall have the right to nominate one blood relative in whose name the Sale Deed for the Apartment can be registered instead of the Vendee, prior to the registration of the Sale Deed. This is limited to only a one-time nomination.</p>
        <p>The Vendee hereby declares that he/she/they will not be entering into any kind of conveyances with third parties with respect to their apartment before the expiry of 24 months from the date of Agreement of Sale. In the event that, the Vendee seeks to transfer his rights concerning the Apartment at any time prior to the registration of the Sale Deed, he can only do so after the stipulated period of 24 months as mentioned here. The Vendee shall not sell the Apartment at any price lower than the prevailing base price of the Developer/AGPA holder for such Apartment and pay an amount of Rs. 150/- per SFT to the Developer/AGPA holder and obtain a No-objection Certificate from the Developer/AGPA holder with respect to such sale by executing required documentation between the Developer/AGPA holder, the Vendee and the third party. Any third party will be bound by the same condition in the event he intends to sell the Apartment. The third party that steps in as a result of such sale shall execute the relevant agreements in the same format as were executed by the Vendees with the Company and shall have all the obligations towards the Developer/AGPA holder as the Vendee had in the first instance.</p>
        <p>The transfer of rights as described above is subject to the following conditions: (i) the Vendee having paid at least 20% of the total consideration from their own capital, and (ii) the Vendee has fulfilled and will full fill, until actual transfer of rights, all their contractual obligations as stipulated in this Agreement.</p>
        <p>7.7 In the event the Developer fails to complete the construction of the Apartment and/or is unable to offer or deliver possession of the Apartment, duly completed in all respects, on or before the date stipulated in Clause 7.1, the Developer shall be liable to compensate the Allottee for such delay. The Developer shall pay compensation at the rate of Rs. 5/- (Rupees Five only) per square foot of the super built-up area per month of delay, calculated from the due date of possession until the actual date on which possession of the Apartment is handed over to the Allottee.</p>

