        <p>(i) DEVELOPER fails to provide ready to move in possession of the flat to the VENDEE/S within the time period specified in para 7.1 or fails to complete the project within the stipulated time disclosed at the time of registration of the project with the Authority. For the purpose of this Para, ready to move in possession&#8217; shall mean that the flat shall be in a habitable condition which is complete in all respects including the provision of all specifications, and facilities, as agreed to between the parties, and for which occupation certificate as the case may be, has been issued by the competent authority.</p>
        <p>(ii) Discontinuance of the DEVELOPER business as a developer on account of suspension or revocation of his registration under the provisions of the Act or the rules and regulations made there under.</p>
        <p>9.2 In case of Default by the DEVELOPER under the conditions listed above, VENDEE/S are entitled to the following:</p>
        <p>(i) Stop making further payments to the DEVELOPER as demanded by the DEVELOPER. If the VENDEE/S stop making payments, the DEVELOPER shall correct the situation by completing the construction milestones and only thereafter the VENDEE/S be required to make the next payment without any interest, or</p>
        <p>(ii) The VENDEE/S shall have the option of terminating the Agreement in which case the DEVELOPER shall be liable to refund the entire money paid by the VENDEE/S under any head whatsoever towards the purchase of the flat, along with interest at the rate prescribed in the rules within ninety days of receiving the termination: Provided that where an VENDEE/S does not intend to withdraw from the project or terminate the Agreement, he shall be paid, by the DEVELOPER, interest at the rate prescribed in the Rules, for every month of delay till the handing over of the possession of the Flat, which shall be paid by the DEVELOPER to the VENDEE/S within ninety days of it becoming due.</p>
        <p>9.3 The VENDEE/S shall be considered under a condition of Default, on the occurrence of the following events:</p>
        <p>(i) In case the VENDEE fails to make payments for 1(One) consecutive demands made by the DEVELOPER as per the Payment Plan annexed hereto, despite having been issued notice in that regard the VENDEE shall be liable to pay interest to the DEVELOPER on the unpaid amount at the rate prescribed in the Rules;</p>
        <p>(ii) In case of default by VENDEE/S under the condition listed above continues for a period beyond 1 (one) consecutive month after notice from the DEVELOPER in this regard, the DEVELOPER may cancel the allotment of Schedule B property in favor of the VENDEE/S and refund the money paid to him by the VENDEE/S by deducting the booking amount and the interest liabilities and this Agreement shall thereupon stand terminated. Provided that the DEVELOPER shall intimate the VENDEE/S about such termination at least thirty days prior to such termination. The amount shall be repaid by the DEVELOPER within a period of ninety days after termination or the date on which the DEVELOPER able to resell the Schedule B Property to other VENDEE/S, whichever is later.</p>

