        <h3>11. MAINTENANCE OF THE SAID BUILDING/FLAT:</h3>
        <p>11.1 The DEVELOPER shall be responsible to provide and maintain essential service in the Project till the taking over or the maintenance of the Project by the Association of VENDEE/S and the cost of maintenance shall be borne by the DEVELOPER and the VENDEE/S, proportionate to the Flats in their respective occupation, provided that the Promoter shall exclusively provide the maintenance services for the Flat till the date on which the Flat is handed over to the VENDEE. After such period, the Association of VENDEE/S shall be responsible for the maintenance of the Flat and Project. The VENDEE/S further agree that the Developer shall be permitted to appoint a Property Management Company (&#8220;PMC&#8221;) for the maintenance. The VENDEE/S agree to enter into a Property Management Agreement with the PMC in the form prescribed by the DEVELOPER/PMC in relation to the provision of such services as and when asked by the DEVELOPER.</p>
        <p>11.2 The facilities like club house and service connections, like water and sewerage supply, which are common shall be maintained by the DEVEOPER till the entire project is completed. The club house and its services shall be subject to user charges as may be fixed by the DEVELOPER of the club house or as the case may be the service provider, from time to time.</p>
        <p>11.3 All other infrastructural facilities, including the equipment like lift, mechanical, electrical or electronic equipment, STP, etc shall be covered by appropriate annual maintenance agreements and insurance agreements with the authorized service providers and the costs of such annual maintenance charges and insurance shall be part of the maintenance charges payable by the occupants. Unless the possession is delivered to the VENDEE, the DEVELOPER shall be the occupant in respect of the flats/buildings in the project.</p>
        <p>11.4 The DEVELPOR/maintenance agency/Association or VENDEE/S shall have right of unrestricted access of all Common areas, covered parking and other parking spaces for providing necessary maintenance services and the VENDEE/S agree to permit the Association of VENDEE/S and/or maintenance agency to enter into the Flat or any part thereof, after due notice and during the normal working hours, unless the circumstances warrant otherwise, with a view to set right any defect.</p>
        <p>11.5 VENDEE/S shall have to pay monthly subscriptions as user charges for various facilities such as Club House, Gym, Swimming Pool, and other specific facilities, etc. to be decided by the DEVELOPER at the time of commencement of Maintenance period.</p>
        <p>11.6 DEVELOPER reserves the right to appoint the various service providers for the given amenities including the duration of such appointments, in the interest of the community. The VENDEE/S hereby agree to abide by the bye-laws of the society, club rules and regulations and shall be liable for all such rules and regulations mentioned in the bye-laws, scope of maintenance and shall support all such amendments to the bye-laws from time to time. Scope of Maintenance as per Schedule E</p>
        <p>11.7 It is agreed by the VENDEE/S that he/she/they shall alone be liable to pay the maintenance charges, irrespective of whether the Flat is occupied or not or occupied by a tenant or any other person. THE Society shall have charge on every Flat for all amounts including the maintenance charges, due from the VENDEE/S or other occupants.</p>
        <p>11.8 During the execution of interiors, the VENDEE/S hereby agree to pay charges towards Debris for a single clearance, fixed electricity charges and also agree to pay towards expenses for maintenance of common areas, till the commencement of pre-paid maintenance. All these payments shall be made either in the name of the DEVELOPER or its nominee.</p>
        <p>11.9 The DEVELOPER reserves the right to maintain the common areas of the community for initial two years from the date of commencement of pre-paid maintenance. The commencement date will be intimated and informed either by the company or its nominee. The VENDEE/S hereby agree to pay an amount of Rs. 4/- per Sft for a period of 2 years on the saleable area of his flat as maintenance and corpus fund charges for common areas and all other facilities (the club house maintenance charges are excluded), payable on demand made by the DEVELOPER, normally &#8216;1&#8217; months before handing over of the flat. The DEVELOPER is also free to increase the charges if the above-mentioned amount does not cover the maintenance expenses of the building.</p>

        <h3>12. DEFECT LIABILITY</h3>
        <p>12.1 It is agreed that in case any structural defect or any other defect in workmanship, quality or provision of services or any other obligations (excluding the under-mentioned in clause no.2) of the DEVELOPER as per the agreement for sale relating to such development is brought to the notice of the DEVELOPER within a period of 5 (five) years by the VENDEE/S from the date of handing over possession, it shall be the duty of the DEVELOPER to rectify such defects without further charge, within 30 (thirty) days, and in the event of DEVELOPER failure to rectify such defects within such time, the aggrieved VENDEE/S shall be entitled to receive appropriate compensation in the manner as provided under the Act.</p>
        <p>12.2. Notwithstanding anything contained in the above clause the following exclusions are made</p>
        <p>a. Equipment (passenger/goods, lifts, generator, motors, STP, transformers, gym equipment, windows, etc.) which carry manufacturer&#8217;s guarantees for a limited period. Thereafter, the welfare association/society shall take annual maintenance contract with the suppliers. The DEVELOPER shall transfer manufacturer&#8217;s guarantees/warrantees to the VENDEE/S or association of VENDEE/S as the case may be.</p>
        <p>b. Fittings related to plumbing, sanitary, electrical switches, public bath fitting, door hardware, etc. having natural wear and tear.</p>
        <p>c. Allowable structural and other deformations including expansion quotient (Tiles, granite, railing, wood doors and Kitchen sink).</p>
        <p>d. The terms of work like painting etc. which are subject to wear and tear.</p>
        <p>12.3. The VENDEE/S shall maintain the flats in good tenantable conditions and carry out the internal repairs for the upkeep of the flats. The association of the VENDEE/S or its assigns shall maintain the services and amenities in good condition and covered with proper AMC and insurance. The obligation of the promoter shall be subject to proper maintenance and upkeep of the flats/services and amenities by the VENDEE/S or the association of VENDEE/S as the case may be.</p>

        <h3>13. RIGHT TO ENTER THE FLAT FOR REPAIRS:</h3>
        <p>The DEVELOPER/maintenance agency/association of VENDEE/S shall have rights of unrestricted access of all common areas, garages/covered parking and parking spaces for providing necessary maintenance services and the VENDEE/S agree to permit the association of VENDEE/S and/or maintenance agency to enter into the Schedule B property or any part thereof, after due notice and during the normal working hours, unless the circumstances warrant otherwise, with a view to set right any defect.</p>

        <h3>14.USAGE:</h3>
        <p>Use of Basement and Service Areas: The basement(s) and service areas, if any, as located within the flats shall be earmarked for purposes such as parking spaces and services including but not limited to electric sub-station, transformer, DG set rooms, underground water tanks, pump rooms, maintenance and service rooms, firefighting and equipment&#8217;s etc and other permitted uses as per plans. The VENDEE/S shall not be permitted to use the services areas and the basements in any manner whatsoever, other than those earmarked as parking formed by the VENDEE/S for rendering maintenance services.</p>

        <h3>15.GENERAL COMPLAINCE WITH RESPECT TO THE FLAT:</h3>
        <p>15.1 Subject to Para 12 above, the VENDEE/S shall, after taking possession, be solely responsible to maintain the Schedule B property at his/her/its own cost, in good repair and condition and shall not do or suffer to be done anything in or to the Building, or the Schedule B property or the staircases, lifts, common passages, corridors, circulation areas, atrium or the compound which may be in violation of any laws or rules of any authority or change or alter or make additions to the Schedule B property and keep the Schedule B property, its walls and partitions, sewers, drains, pipe and appurtenances thereto or belonging thereto, in good and tenantable repair and maintain the same in a fit and proper condition and ensure that the support, shelter, etc. of the Building is not in any way damaged or jeopardized.</p>
        <p>15.2 The VENDEE/S further undertake, assure and guarantee that he/she would not put any sign-based/name play, neon light, publicity material or advertisement material etc. on the face/f&#225;&#231;ade of the building or anywhere on the exterior of the Project, buildings therein or common areas. The VENDEE/S shall also not change the color scheme of the outer walls or painting of the exterior side of the window or carry out any change in the exterior elevation or design. Further, the VENDEE/S shall not store any hazardous or combustible goods in Schedule B property or place any heavy material in the common passages or staircase of the building. The VENDEE/S shall also not remove any wall, including the outer and load bearing wall of the Schedule B property.</p>
        <p>15.3 The VENDEE/S shall plan and distribute its electrical load in conformity with the electrical systems installed by the DEVELOPER and thereafter the Association of VENDEE/S and/or maintenance agency appointed by Association of VENDEE/S. The VENDEE/S shall be responsible for any loss or damages arising out of breach of any of the aforesaid conditions.</p>
        <p>15.4 The VENDEE/S shall pay user charges in respect of the Clubhouse, Gym, Swimming pool and all other facilities mentioned in Schedule-D annexed hereto provided by the DEVELOPER or to its nominee or to the Society as per the usage under the Clubhouse rules and regulations and other notices given from time to time. Such user charges shall be paid to the DEVELOPER or its nominees who are the core service providers.</p>
        <p>15.5 Any type of modifications, changes, variations and alterations to the structural, elevation and architectural features shall not be permitted as the construction has been done using Shear Wall Technology and changes shall cause structural damage.</p>
        <p>15.6 The VENDEE/S shall not, at any time, demolish or be a cause to demolish their Flat or any part of the building including the common areas such as staircase, Verandah, parking places, etc. which are likely to cause injury or damage to the structure of the building. The VENDEE/S shall not make or be a cause to make any additions or alterations or any new connections of any nature, whatsoever, contrary to the plan for their Flat or to any part of the building. The VENDEE/S shall not close the balconies and parking with grills or any other partitions or fix sliding/fixed windows to the balconies/service areas or make any additions and alterations in the elevation and shall not alter the exterior of the building, including color scheme without the unanimous approval of the Association.</p>
        <p>15.7 The VENDEE/S shall keep their Flat as well as partition walls, drains, drainpipes, water pipelines and the appurtenances thereto in good tenable condition so as to support shelter and protect all parts of the building and also for good utility and occupation.</p>
        <p>15.8 The VENDEE/S shall use the common over-head tank provided for, along with other Flat owners of the building, and agree to pay the water charges as and when levied, proportionately as per the reading of water meter. The VENDEE/S agree to fix the air conditioner units, both the outdoor and indoor units at the designated location as shown/earmarked in the flat only. The VENDEE/S cannot request for the same to be shifted for any reason.</p>
        <p>15.9 The VENDEE/S also covenants that they will not throw dust, rubbish, rags, waste, spit or permit the same to be thrown in the compound or in any portion of the said building which may cause damage or inconvenience to other occupants of the building. It is hereby specifically agreed by the VENDEE/S that will dry their clothes only in the Utility areas. The VENDEE/S will not dry any clothes on the parapet walls of Utility area or utilize common areas such as the terrace to dry their clothes and are required to use specifically designed stand/apparatus/pulley systems for the same. The VENDEE/S shall not keep door mats, shoe racks, footwear or any kind of personal material or their belongings in any of the common areas including the corridors, parking areas, terrace areas, etc.</p>
        <p>15.10. The VENDEE/S and Association of VENDEE/S agree not to dry clothes in the Sit out, place pots, clad the walls in any material, paint the walls in a different colour, install false ceiling in Balcony, fix cupboard/racks or make any modifications to the Sit outs. The DEVELOPER reserves the right to remove any such installations/modifications at any point of time till the complete hand over of the project to the Association.</p>
        <p>15.11. The VENDEE/S or Association of VENDEE/S agree that corridor area will not be used fix cupboards, shoe rack, racks, place pots or undertake any modification to the way it was handed over. Further, the VENDEE/S and Association of ALLOTTES agree that no changes to the main door including change in color, height and width, installation of additional screen door over the main door will be undertaken by them. The VENDEE/S and Association of ALLOTTES also agree that corridor walls including those next to the main door will not be painted in a different color, cladded with material or make any necessary changes to the way it is handed over at time of completion.</p>
        <p>15.12. The VENDEE/S and Association of ALLOTTES agree that their name board outside their flat will be in accordance to the design provided by the DEVELOPER. Further they agree that no light fixtures or signages can be installed outside the main door or corridor.</p>
        <p>15.13. The VENDEE/S hereby agree that they will use the said Flat for residential purposes only and shall not use for commercial purposes such as office space, clinics, consultancies, display centers, service flats. or permit the same to be used for any other purpose which may likely to cause inconvenience to the neighboring occupants of the building nor shall it be used for any illegal or immoral purposes but strictly for residential use and if it is let out, should be utilized for the residential purpose only.</p>
        <p>15.14. It is agreed between the parties that the Area shown in the Schedule B as a Verandah area attached to the entrance of the Flat shall be for the exclusive utilization of the VENDEE/S and no third parties shall be allowed to utilize the same without the express authorization of the VENDEE/S. However, it is specifically agreed by the VENDEES that this &#8220;Sit-Out&#8221; area shall not be covered or barricaded in any manner. Provided that, in the event that the VENDEE/S are particularly of the intent to cover / barricade the area, the same may be permitted by the Owners&#8217; Association that is in charge of the maintenance of the Project, on collection of a sum of not less than Rs. 20,00,000/- (Rupees Twenty Lakhs only), as may be stipulated by the Association and all and any such amounts received shall be remitted into the Corpus Account of the Project, for being utilized as such, for such purposes that the Corpus amounts may be utilized.</p>
        <p>Planter boxes and windows are staggered and positioned differently for each Flat and they will be fixed as per the architectural elevation design.</p>
        <p>15.15 Plants to be planted in the planted box will be defined by the DEVELOPER and has to be strictly followed by the VENDEE/S.</p>

