        <h3>19. MISCELLANEOUS:</h3>
        <p>19.1 The Parties hereby agree that in case the VENDEE/S are availing a housing loan/loan from any bank/Financial institution/Non-Banking Financial Corporation Financier (the &#8220;Bank&#8221;), a Tri-partite Agreement, as per the draft provided by the Bank and agreed by the DEVELOPER shall be executed by and between the Bank, the DEVELOPER and the VENDEE/S. In any event, the VENDEE/S will finance the margin money, and the loan will be paid directly from the Bank to the DEVELOPER. The VENDEE/S acknowledge that the VENDEE/S obligation to pay the total sale consideration as mentioned in this Agreement shall be independent and exclusive liability, which is independent of the bank loan obtained by the VENDEE/S, such that, if the VENDEE/S are unable to obtain a bank loan or having obtained a bank loan, the Bank is not disbursing the money, the VENDEE/S SHALL be independently liable to pay the sale consideration to the DEVELOPER. The DEVELOPER shall not be responsible in any way if the VENDEE/S do not succeed in receiving a loan from the Bank.</p>
        <p>19.2. The building is named and called as &#8220;THE LEGACEY&#8221; and the DEVELOPER can erect display boards/name boards as per their commercial and branding requirements on a permanent basis. The name board of the builders will be displayed permanently at the site and the VENDEE/S have no objection to the same.</p>
        <p>19.3 Whereas the Vendee was clearly informed and acknowledges that the Developer has applied for permission to construct two additional floors, i.e., the 23rd and 24th floors, above the sanctioned Ground + 22 floors, by utilizing Transferable Development Rights (TDR) purchased by the Developer. The Vendee agrees that the said additional floors (23rd and 24th floors), shall be the exclusive property of the Developer, and the Vendee shall have no right, title, interest, or claim of any nature whatsoever in respect thereof. The Vendee further has no objection to the allocation and distribution of the proportionate undivided share of land among the purchasers/owners of the sanctioned Ground + 22 floors, as may be finalized upon approval of the revised plan by the competent authority. The Vendee undertakes to sign and furnish all documents required by competent authorities, for obtaining approvals, sanctions, for the said additional floors, without objection to the developer.</p>
        <p>19.4 The VENDEE/S will not be allowed to start interior works until the construction of flat is totally constructed and completed. Once, the flat is handed over to the VENDEE/S for interiors means and includes that the flat is fully finished and formalities of handover is complete, irrespective of whether or not the flat is ready for living. Interiors will be allowed only after handing over/taking over of the Flat. The Interiors shall be done between 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM only. THE VENDEE/S has to pay a penalty to the society for interiors done beyond 4 months of handing over.</p>
        <p>19.5 The Developer/Promoter reserves the right to maintain the common areas of the community for initial two years from the date of commencement of pre-paid maintenance. The commencement date will be notified either by the Developer or its nominee at an appropriate time. The purchaser hereby agrees to pay an amount of Rs.96/- per Sq. Ft. Plus 18% GST for the saleable area as maintenance charges for maintenance of common areas for the period of two (2) years. The Water charges are NOT included in the said maintenance charges. (payable on demand made by the developer, normally '3' months before handing over). During the execution of interiors, the purchaser/s hereby agree/s to pay the fixed one-time Move in charges @ Rs.25,000/- Plus 18% GST; towards clearance of debris, Fixed Electricity charges during for 3 Months from the date of Possession, thereafter the charges for Electricity shall be applicable based on units consumed as per the electric meter reading. The Vendee(s)/Purchaser(s) also agrees to pay Rs. 2/- per Sq. Ft. plus 18% GST of the saleable area per month, on monthly basis, towards interim maintenance of common areas and utilities, till such time of commencement of pre-paid maintenance for two years. This interim maintenance is payable irrespective of completion of interior works and all these payments shall be made either in the name of developer or its nominee. The VENDEE/S shall pay an amount of Rs. 25,000/- plus 18% GST towards legal and documentation charges plus applicable taxes at the time of execution of Sale Deed Registration.</p>
        <p>If any water problem arises due to insufficient depth of the present bore well, the VENDEE(S) hereby agreed to share proportionately the expenses/cost incurred for increasing the depth of the present Bore-well or for digging new Bore-well. The Developer will not be responsible for the same and all the Flat Owners of the building shall collectively bear the same.</p>
        <p>19.6 It is agreed that the parking places will be allotted to the VENDEE/S through the lottery method.</p>
        <p>19.7 It is agreed by both the parties that the Developer will provide CCTV surveillance only for drive ways, entry &amp; exit ramps of parking area. No individual parking slots will be covered by CCTV.</p>
        <p>19.8 All the owners/residents must park their vehicles in the parking lots allotted to them and they must not park their vehicles in any of the open areas of the building, setbacks, or in the parking lots of other owners/residents.</p>

        <h3>20. FORMATION OF ASSOCIATION OF VENDEE/S</h3>
        <p>The DEVELOPER shall take the following steps to enable formation of an Association of VENDEE/S under S.11(4)(e) of the Act:</p>
        <p>With respect to a real estate project, the DEVELOPER shall submit an application to the Registrar for registration of the Association of VENDEE/S as a society under the Telangana/A.P Societies Registration Act, 2001 (as applicable to the state of Telangana), within two months from the date on which the occupation certificate in respect of such project is issued and a minimum of sixty per cent of the total VENDEE/S in such a project have taken possession and the DEVELOPER has received the full consideration from such VENDEE/S. All the VENDEE/S on payment of full consideration shall become members of such Association of VENDEE/S formed by the DEVELOPER applications, petitions, for forming an association.</p>
        <p>The Association will have to be formed as per the above clause, however, the decision with regard to continuation of maintenance by the PROMOTER/DEVELOPER, will be at that point of time vest with the Association. If the DEVELOPER fails to form the Association of VENDEE/S, the Authority shall by an order direct the DEVELOPER to apply for formation of such Association or may authorize the VENDEE/S to apply for the formation of the said Association.</p>
        <p>Notwithstanding any other rule, after conveying the title to the Association of VENDEE/S under S.17, the DEVELOPER shall continue to have the rights and entitlement to advertise, market, book, sell or offer to sell or allot to person to purchase any flat or building or plot which is still not sold or allotted and shall be deemed to have been allowed to do so by the Association of DEVELOPER without any restriction or entry of the building and development of common areas.</p>

